course: dictionary
lesson: 14370
title: Optional: you can choose
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Some things must be done, and some things are your choice. Optional means you can choose to do or have something, but you do not have to. «The extra puzzle sheet is optional.» You may do it if you want, and nobody will make you.
explain: Look at the words around it for clues. «Homework is compulsory, but the challenge questions are optional.» Compulsory means you must do it, so the contrast tells you that optional means you may choose. Always check: does your meaning still fit the sentence?
explain: Optional is an adjective, so it describes a thing such as a task, an extra or a choice. In a shop you might read, «Sauce is optional at the burger bar, and it costs extra.» You can choose the sauce or leave it.
fact: Optional means something you can choose to do or have, but you do not have to.
fact: The opposite of optional is compulsory, which means you must do it.
fact: «Optional» can describe school work, such as «optional homework».
fact: «Optional» extension tasks give extra challenge to anyone who wants it.
fact: Extras like sauce or gift wrapping are often optional, and they may cost more.
exercise: «The extra puzzle sheet is optional.» What does optional mean? | You must finish it before lunch | *You can choose to do it, but you do not have to | You are not allowed to look at it | It is a very long puzzle
exercise: «Homework is compulsory, but the challenge questions are optional.» What is the opposite of optional? | Quiet | Extra | Hard | *Compulsory
exercise: At the burger bar the sauce is optional and costs extra. Is the sauce something you must have? | No, sauce is never sold | Yes, every burger must have sauce | Yes, sauce is free and compulsory | *No, you can choose it or leave it
test: «Wearing a costume to the play is optional.» Does Priya have to wear a costume? | Yes, the teacher insists | She must wear it every day | *No, she can choose | Yes, it is compulsory
test: Which sentence shows something optional? | Swimming is compulsory on Fridays | The register is taken at nine each morning | *Joining the choir is optional, so you can join if you like | Every pupil must wear a uniform
exam: Which is the best meaning of optional? | *Something you can choose to do or have | Something you must do every day | Something you are not allowed to do | Something that everyone in the class does
